[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3053903917","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108429#issuecomment-3053903917","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108429","id":3053903917,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62BuAt","user":{"login":"simpkins","id":163549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins","html_url":"https://github.com/simpkins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T20:23:46Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T20:23:46Z","body":"I was able to work around the command line to long errors on Linux and Android by updating `$ARCOM` to use `$(TEMPFILE)`, so I submitted a PR to merge these libraries into one: #108426\n\nIn the future it might be possible to clean up the dependencies a little bit to split these into smaller libraries again, but we would probably also need to improve the build system to ensure that people cannot add incorrect dependencies again.   One way to do this would be to set `CPPPATH` so that code in `core/` cannot see headers in `main/` or `scene/`, etc.  Doing this today would probably require copying the header files to a separate directory so that we can have a directory with only the headers that should be visible to the current library, and adding that to CPPPATH rather than adding the repository root directory to CPPPATH.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3053903917/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3053988277","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108429#issuecomment-3053988277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108429","id":3053988277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62CCm1","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T20:58:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T20:58:21Z","body":"There's absolutely a problem with the `#include` order in the repo as it currently exists, and it's very much dumb luck that so much of this functions at all. I'm STRONGLY in favor of a major structural overhaul if it meant ensuring these kinds of dependency issues would be sorted for good, though that very well may be 5.0 territory","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3053988277/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056033348","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108429#issuecomment-3056033348","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108429","id":3056033348,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62J15E","user":{"login":"ze2j","id":46556066,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTU2MDY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46556066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j","html_url":"https://github.com/ze2j","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T07:25:02Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T07:25:02Z","body":"For argument list too long issue, one solution is to use a file as argument of `ar`, see [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/issues/1729#issuecomment-2703282432).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056033348/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056809149","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108429#issuecomment-3056809149","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108429","id":3056809149,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62MzS9","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T10:26:49Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T10:26:49Z","body":"We happened to be talking about this in a meeting just yesterday. We agreed it's a good goal to 'harden' dependencies, such that e.g. `core` cannot depend on `main`. We're open to suggestions for how best to achieve this.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056809149/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058421053","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108429#issuecomment-3058421053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108429","id":3058421053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62S809","user":{"login":"simpkins","id":163549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins","html_url":"https://github.com/simpkins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T18:04:14Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T18:04:14Z","body":"In the short term the simplest solution would probably be to just add hook that scans the diff and looks for includes that shouldn't be present.  This should probably be pretty low-overhead to add to both the pre-commit hooks and the static_checks workflow.\n\ne.g., just as a dumb proof-of-concept:\n`git diff 99666de00fb^ 99666de00fb | awk '/^\\+\\+\\+ b\\// { file_start_line=$0; if ($0 ~ /^+++ b\\/core\\//) { in_core=1 } else { in_core=0 } }; /^\\+#include \"(main|scene|servers)\\// { if (in_core) { print \"bad include: \" file_start_line \" : \" $0 } }'`\nIn practice you would want to implement this check in Python or some other sane language, which will be a little more overhead but probably still be fine for a pre-commit hook.\n\nThis would require manually maintaining the list of rules to enforce in this check, rather than having it automatically deduced from the build system, but that probably is fine in practice.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058421053/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058450595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108429#issuecomment-3058450595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108429","id":3058450595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62TECj","user":{"login":"simpkins","id":163549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins","html_url":"https://github.com/simpkins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T18:14:05Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T18:14:05Z","body":"I think it might also be worth coming up with some sort of plan/documentation for dependencies between modules and the central godot (core+scene+servers) code.  Most modules depend on the central code, and aren't used by the central code.  However, there are a handful of modules that are used by core, scene, and servers:\n* modules/regex: used by core/io/logger.cpp and scene/gui/rich_text_label.cpp\n* modules/mbedtls: used by core/crypto/SCsub and core/crypto/crypto.cpp\n* modules/svg: used by scene/resources/svg_texture.cpp\n* modules/glslang: used by servers/rendering/\n\nIt seems like it might be worth separating the module types somehow, and having clear separation between modules that depend on the central godot code and should not be used by it, vs modules that the central code uses and which should not depend on the central code themselves.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058450595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058653363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108429#issuecomment-3058653363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108429","id":3058653363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62T1iz","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T19:11:07Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T19:11:07Z","body":"I should mention we already have a plan to merge [`STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_TYPE`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107587), which will allow us to assert include order at the header / class level.\n\n> I think it might also be worth coming up with some sort of plan/documentation for dependencies between modules and the central godot (core+scene+servers) code. \n\nWe do have some documentation for this, for example the [architecture diagram](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/development/core_and_modules/godot_architecture_diagram.html). But I don't know how up-to-date it is (and for that matter, how up-to-date anything we make for this will stay over the years).\nPractically, it might be best to establish and assert the dependencies at a module level, making individual decisions, and then generate graphs from that to put on the documentation pages, rather than the other way around.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058653363/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]